{title: Frosty the Snowman}

{capo-guitar: 1}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[A]Frosty the snowman was a [D]jolly happy [A]soul
With [D]corn cob pipe and a [A]button nose
And two [E]eyes made out of [E7]coal

[A]Frosty the snowman is a [D]fairy tale they [A]say
He was [D]made of snow but the [A]children know
how he [E]came to life one [A]day

There [D]must have been some [A]magic in that [Bm]old silk [E]cap they [A]found
For [B]when they placed it on his head he be[E]gan to dance a[E7]round

[A]Frosty the snowman was [D]alive as he could [A]be
And the [D]children say he could [A]laugh and play
Just the [E]same as you and [A]me

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus"}

[A]Thumpety-thump-thump
[A]Thumpety-thump-thump
[A]Look at Frosty [E]go

[E7]Thumpety-thump-thump
[E7]Thumpety-thump-thump
Over the hills of [A]snow

{end_of_chorus}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[A]Frosty the snowman knew the [D]sun was hot that [A]day
So he [D]said let’s run and we'll [A]have some fun
Now be[E]fore I melt a[E7]way

[A]Down to the village with a [D]broomstick in his [A]hand
Running [D]here and there all a[A]round the square
Saying [E]"Catch me if you [A]can!"

He [D]led them down the [A]streets of town [Bm]right to the [E]traffic [A]cop
And he [B]only paused a moment when he [E]heard him holler, [E7]"Stop!"

[A]Frosty the snowman had to [D]hurry on his [A]way
But he [D]waved goodbye saying, [A]"Don’t you cry!"
{comment: ritard}
I’ll be [E]back a[E7]gain some [A]day

{end_of_verse}